{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/395788-laments-in-wraith-20","id":395788,"title":"Laments in Wraith 20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-06T20:25:00-08:00","id":395788,"title":"Laments in Wraith 20","content":"Just trying to air my thoughts here\u2026<br /> <br /> We\u2019ve got material in Orpheus appearing in Wraith 20; and from some recent stuff I\u2019ve been hearing, it looks like it may be a bit more detailed than \u201chere\u2019s what the Orpheus corporation looks like in the context of Wraith\u201d \u2014 we may actually be getting agents of Orpheus as playable characters. With that in mind, some thoughts about elements of Orpheus and how they might fit into Wraith:<br /> <br /> <b><u>Laments</u></b><br /> Orpheus has four Laments: two kinds of Projectors (Skimmers and Sleepers) and two types of Ghosts (Spirits and Hues). As presented in <b>Orpheus</b>, these are all treated as slight variations on a shared set of concepts and mechanics: all four have Shades and Horrors; all four get the same set of default abilities (e.g., <i>Detect Nature Group</i>, <i>Misery Loves Company</i>, <i>Sense Lifeline</i>, <i>Sever the Strand</i> and <i>Thievery</i>). <br /> <br /> \u2014 So the first and perhaps most important question to answer is this: are Spirits and Wraiths the same thing? <br /> <br /> If the are, then you\u2019re going to have to bend parts of <b>Orpheus</b> to fit into <b>Wraith</b>, or vice versa. If they <i>aren\u2019t</i>, then you need to explain how and why they\u2019re different. I may come back to the \u201cthey\u2019re different\u201d option later; but for now, I\u2019d like to address the implications of them being the same. <br /> <br /> \u2022 First, there\u2019s the matter that wraiths have Shadows while Spirits have Spectre nemeses. Easily enough addressed: the Fifth Great Maelstrom caused some metaphysical changes to the Shadowlands and their denizens, and the \u201cSpectre nemesis\u201d is a post-5GM phenomenon. That means that in pre-5GM games (which I expect to be the default in <b>Wr20</b>), Spirits have Shadows rather than Spectre nemeses. Easy enough. <br /> \u2022 If Spirits and Wraiths are the same thing, then either Spirits have Arcanoi or Wraiths have Horrors. This being Wraith, I would be shocked if it were the former. So far so good. <br /> \u2022 many other elements of Wraith and Orpheus are direct parallels, such as Pathos and Vitality or Angst and Spite. As with the Arcanoi/Horrors thing, the Wraith versions win out. <br /> \u2022 There are a few things that Wraith has that Orpheus doesn\u2019t, such as Passions. Again, Wraith takes the fore and Spirits pick up these traits. <br /> \u2022 Where it gets tricky is when a Spirit has traits that a Wraith lacks: default abilities such as <i>Detect Nature Group</i>, or Shades. My gut reaction would be to drop these things for the same reason: Wraith trumps Orpheus. Maybe include them in a post-5GM Shard alongside the aforementioned \u201cSpectre nemeses\u201d. <br /> <br /> But it was recently pointed out that these things in particular \u2014 Shades and the Nature Groups on which they\u2019re based \u2014 are so important to the Orpheus experience that an effort ought to be made to include them. This introduces a dilemma: how to make Shades a part of playing a Spirit who works with Orpheus without forcing all wraiths to partake of the \u201cNature Groups and Shades\u201d concepts and mechanics? The only answer I can think of is \u201cmake it an optional system that the Storyteller can use or ignore as he sees fit.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u2014 Hues are the next Lament that needs to be considered. Like Spirits, they\u2019re ghosts; but they\u2019re ghosts of people who were subject to a drug called \u201cpigment\u201d (which, later in the Orpheus series, is revealed to include the essence of spectres in its manufacturing process). Mechanically, Hues differ from Spirits in that instead of having a Spectre nemesis, they have limitations on their Vitality. How to translate this to Wraith? First, Hues don\u2019t have Shadows; that\u2019s something unique to the aforementioned Spirit Lament a.k.a. wraiths. That doesn\u2019t mean that Hues don\u2019t have Angst; only that it doesn\u2019t manifest through a separate consciousness. So no Shadowguiding for Hues. Guidelines should be provided for how to handle this, especially since said guidelines will be useful for the projector Laments as well. As for the limit on Vitality: a literal translation of this rule would be to cap Pathos to its initial value when the character is created. But I think we might be able to do better: tie it to Passions instead, giving Hues fewer dots of starting Passions than wraiths get, and making it harder for them to raise their Passions. <br /> <br /> \u2014 for the projector Laments, I\u2019d like to start with Skimmers. Skimmers are living people with a natural ability to project their spirits out of their bodies and travel the land of the dead. The cost to them is that damage to their projected form manifests on their body: lost Corpus doubles as lost Health. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m starting with Skimmers because I think they\u2019re most likely to be wraith-like. Sure, they don\u2019t have Shadows (probably); but they very likely <i>do</i> have Passions, Pathos, Angst, Tethers, and so on \u2014 basically, they\u2019re a bit like the Risen, but with a living body instead of a reanimated corpse; and again, no Shadow. <br /> <br /> \u2014 Sleepers are probably the same as Sleepers, save for two things: damage to Corpus <i>doesn\u2019t</i> translate to damage to health; and their ability to project is totally dependent on climbing into a high-tech coffin. <br /> <br /> These are just cursory thoughts; I\u2019m sure I\u2019ve overlooked something important.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T20:31:32-08:00","id":395799,"title":"","content":"A contrary view: if Spirits and Wraiths are two different things, many of the mechanical issues presented above are trivially solved: Laments can be as much like <b>Orpheus</b> as one wants them to be. The cost to this, though, lies in explaining how and why Spirits and Wraiths differ. Hues differ from wraiths in that Pigment was involved in their creation; projectors differ from wraiths in that they\u2019re living people who visit the land of the dead. But what about spirits? They were designed in <b>Orpheus</b> to inhabit precisely the same conceptual space that wraiths occupy: ordinary ghosts. If they\u2019re <i>not</i> that in Wraith 20, then what <i>are</i> they?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-06T23:19:43-08:00","id":395867,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/395788-laments-in-wraith-20?p=395799#post395799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A contrary view: if Spirits and Wraiths are two different things, many of the mechanical issues presented above are trivially solved: Laments can be as much like <b>Orpheus</b> as one wants them to be. The cost to this, though, lies in explaining how and why Spirits and Wraiths differ. Hues differ from wraiths in that Pigment was involved in their creation; projectors differ from wraiths in that they\u2019re living people who visit the land of the dead. But what about spirits? They were designed in <b>Orpheus</b> to inhabit precisely the same conceptual space that wraiths occupy: ordinary ghosts. If they\u2019re <i>not</i> that in Wraith 20, then what <i>are</i> they?</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps the 5GM caused more changes for wraiths than any previous GM had ever caused- separating the shadow from the wraith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T06:33:41-08:00","id":396239,"title":"","content":"\u2026which does nothing for explaining how things work in pre-5GM games that involve Orpheus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T07:16:52-08:00","id":396322,"title":"","content":"Hi there! In my opinion, the split between the shadow and the wraith was due to 'technical' reasons. First, it would have been unfair to force the wraith players to deal with a shadow (as a Lament disavantage) whereas the other Laments simply implied 'mechanical' disavantages. Secondly, taking in account the plot and the fact that Grandma and the malfeens spy the collective mind of specters, it would have been almost impossible for a regular wraith to go through the story with a regular shadow, therefore the developers went for this split.<br /> Regarding your question, in my opinion the possible answer lies in the background: do you play Orpheus in Wraith20 or do you use Wraith20 for Orpheus? Was there a 6th great maelstrom or do Stygia and the Shadowland Necropolis still exist? Because this split could be due to metaphysical consequences of the 6th maelstrom, a bit like the reinforcement of the Shroud and the Tempest due to the 3rd maelstrom. Or maybe the Ferrymen (known to be split from their Pasiphae) managed to settle a powerful ritual and to extend their condition to the whole underworld?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4701-dam","name":"Dam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4701_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T07:20:24-08:00","id":396326,"title":"","content":"Sorry, not very familiar with Orpheus. <br /> <br /> But if we assume Spirits = Wraiths, and any differences between the two are a result of 5GM, then including Orpheus in Wraith20 would mean to me that the space once inhabited by spirits is now inhabited by wraiths and function like wraiths because this is Wraith20. Any differences between Spirits and Wraiths don't exist because for all intents and purposes Spirits don't exist yet.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I misinterpreted your last question as rhetorical... from what I know of Orpheus, having both Spirits and Wraiths inhabiting the same setting doesn't seem to make a whole lot of sense to me. As far as I know these two takes on ghosts are mutually exclusive... either they have shadows, or they have doppelgangers. <br /> <br /> Perhaps they could include Doppelgangers as a &quot;setting dial&quot; alternative to shadowguiding. <br /> <br /> But they would have to invent some reason why some ghosts are Wraiths and others are Spirits, and outside of 5GM I don't know what could explain this.<br /> <br /> The other 3 Laments are altogether something new, and can work the way they always have as a separate sort of splat, or maybe they can be adapted to better fit the Wraith system, with Arcanoi instead of Horrors, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1078-froggy711","name":"Froggy711","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1078_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}